677: ## Wire contracts (documented in P0 before tests)
678: 
679: Phase A
680: - `SessionLogSubmitResult` 201 body adds `turns: [{ requestId, outcome, storedStatus, reason }]`, `outcome` in `created|merged|skipped_terminal` (no `skipped_duplicate`; an identical resubmit is `merged` with reason `no_change`; duplicate requestIds in one submission are applied last-wins with one outcome each). MCP `sessionlog_submit` returns `{ success, id, turns }`. Status code stays 201 (late-hook snapshot protection).
681: - Plugin receipt on `skipped_terminal`: `code: skipped_terminal`, `persisted: false`, `storedStatus`, `reason`; verb returns false; exit 1; failsafe cleared. The `appendDialog` and `setTurnTitle` receipts map their own route results: 200 `persisted`, 404 `request_unknown`, an outage `queued` with a failsafe record keyed by the bound requestId; a submit answered without per-turn outcomes is reported `outcomeVerified: false` and never as a confirmed close (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-004-AC005).
682: - Hook statuses: new `system-event-skipped`, `turn-open-contended`, `turn-open-failed` (with reason `nonce_source_missing` or the server code); `turn-already-open` when a mint returns `merged` (same nonce) for an in-progress turn, with two exceptions: on copilot and classic cline a `merged` result of a new invocation fails the host session closed under the equal-field rule (`turn_logging_unsupported`, `indistinguishable_arrival`), while a stored mint retry or failsafe drain binds normally; and a `merged` result for a turn that is already terminal reports its `storedStatus` and the hook neither makes it the write target nor adds it to the open list or the stop ledger (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001-AC002).
683: - Stop gate: blocks `turn_in_progress` for a delivered-ledger turn still in_progress (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003-AC004), blocks `turn_withdrawn_unclosed` through the separate scan of `withdrawn` entries still in_progress, and only warns for a minted request still `queued` although its server turn is in_progress (`StopGate_QueuedInProgressServerTurn_NoBlockBeforeDelivery_Warns`); in a host session with `unsupportedSince`, a turn whose close is captured as an `unsupported_session` failsafe record is warned with the cause instead, and before that its remedy names only the missing model evidence, the missing `requestClass` (from S8/S9), and the close call, the terminal reviews being judged at the drain, FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC001; outside `unsupportedSince`, a turn whose model close is held in the ordinary failsafe by a transport outage is warned as degraded persistence instead, and its ledger entry stays until the server confirms the close), `session_turn_completion_gate` (a turn whose most recent close the server refused with that code, recorded locally from the server response; such a turn is still in progress; no marker condition, FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC003), failed build after edits (existing), stale session (existing); blocks `turn_withdrawn_unclosed` (a withdrawn queued request still in_progress); warns on exactly the FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC005 list; re-evaluates on every Stop, including `stop_hook_active=true`, blocking again while turns are open and recording `stop_gate_overridden_by_host` if the host stops anyway; passes with `{}` and clears closed entries. Auto-close removed. Block text: `session_turn_stop_gate: <n> turn(s) are not closed correctly:` then one line per turn `<id> (<code>): <remedy>`, then `The stop gate never closes turns for you.`; each turn's remedy accumulates every unmet prerequisite of that turn, in this order: for a turn whose most recent close the server refused with `session_turn_completion_gate`, the server's missing items first (in place of the locally computed `requestClass` and review items); at least one model-authored action, designDecision, or commit (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC002); `requestClass` (from S8/S9, when the plugin's requestClass and recordReview verbs ship); the terminal reviews the completion gate names (from S8/S9, when the plugin's requestClass and recordReview verbs ship, gate order; before S10 the server accepts those writes, so following the remedy literally still passes); then the single close call valid for its status: `workflow.sessionlog.failTurn` with reason 'withdrawn before delivery' for a withdrawn request, otherwise `workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn` (or `failTurn` if the work failed), passing requestId <id>. Following a turn's remedy literally makes the next Stop pass for that turn, including a Code turn that lacks both model evidence and terminal reviews (`StopGate_EachRemedyFollowedLiterally_NextStopPasses`, `StopGate_CodeTurn_MissingEvidenceAndReviews_AccumulatedRemedy_NextStopPasses`).
684: - Ingress mint (D1): `POST /qbrainai/sessionlog/{agent}/{sessionId}/mint` (also `/mcpserver/sessionlog/...`), client `MintTurnAsync` and REPL `workflow.sessionlog.mintTurn` (hook and adapter callers only; no MCP tool), exactly as TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-004 AC-005 specifies: first mint 201 `outcome: created`; same nonce in the same session 200 `outcome: merged` with the same requestId. Failsafe mint record: `{ method: workflow.sessionlog.mintTurn, params: { ingressNonce, queryTitle, queryText, model, planFile: None, todoId: None }, provisionalRequestId: pending-<nonce>, binding: { hostSessionKey, keySource, ingressNonce, requestId: pending-<nonce>, boundAtUtc }, plus the root-id envelope of FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC009 }` (hooks send the `None` sentinels; a later update sets the real values). Drain order: the plugin first replays an idempotent session open for the record's envelope `mcpSessionId`, then the mint; a `session_not_open` refusal is final only after that session open is confirmed (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001-AC008).
685: - Arrival bridge (D5): `sessions/<key>/arrival-bridge.pid` and the `turn-state.yaml` lifecycle below (no separate offset file); the bridge is the only minter on claude-code and claude-cowork, a fail-closed host session records `unsupportedSince: { causeOffset, causeOperation, reason }`, and a session-log verb applies, before binding, only the complete records that end at or before the transcript length it recorded when it started (D2); the Stop hook (from its payload `transcript_path`) and SessionStart apply pending records through `Sync-PluginArrivalLog` the same way, up to the transcript length at their own start, so a dead bridge never hides a delivered request from the Stop gate.
686: - Plugin per-turn store: `turns/<requestId>.yaml` (one file per turn, own lock `turns/<requestId>.lock`), `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/turn-state.yaml` `{ writeTarget: { requestId, deliveredAtUtc, source: prompt-hook | dequeue | absorbed-mid-turn } | null, openDelivered: [requestId], queue: [{ kind: request | system, requestId and nonce (request entries only), enqueueOffset, enqueueTimestamp, promptSha256, state: queued | delivered | withdrawn, stateOffset, mintedAtUtc }], appliedThroughOffset, mcpSessionId }, every entry also carrying the root ids of FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC009` (written only by the writers TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003 AC-007 lists: the arrival bridge, or a verb, the Stop hook, or SessionStart applying pending transcript records through `Sync-PluginArrivalLog`, the prompt hook on hosts without a bridge, the first-ingress writer on hosts without a SessionStart event (A8: it records the host session's `mcpSessionId` under the host session lock before the mint), the close verbs, the failsafe drain (alias rebind), the Stop gate (clearing confirmed-closed ledger entries and recording `stop_gate_overridden_by_host`), the first verb or hook that records `unsupportedSince` with reason `duplicate_prompt_hook`, and SessionStart recording the host session's own `mcpSessionId` and clearing a cause its rule allows, each write one atomic replace under `turn-open.lock`; the bridge, the mint, and every verb read the MCP session id only from this file, the workspace-level `session-state.yaml` is a legacy file never used for targeting, and the rotated-sessionId rebind of `repl-invoke.ps1:1954-1965` is never applied to per-turn files), `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/ended.yaml`, `current-turn.yaml` kept only as a read-only legacy status file `{ turnRequestId }` never used for targeting, the stop ledger as `ledger: [...]` inside `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/turn-state.yaml` (one file per host session, so an entry is added in the same atomic replace that delivers its request and advances `appliedThroughOffset`, never at mint; a crash leaves both or neither), all under `turn-open.lock`. No prompt ledger and no dedupe window. Every verb invocation carries a binding `{ hostSessionKey, keySource, ingressNonce, requestId, boundAtUtc }` (C4) captured once at start (D2) and stored in its persist and failsafe records; failsafe paths and fingerprints include the bound requestId. Verbs accept an explicit `requestId` override, required while two or more delivered requests are open (`request_ambiguous`, D9); unknown ids are refused with `request_unknown`.
687: 
688: Phase B turn shape (additive on `UnifiedRequestEntryDto`, server and client)
689: ```json
690: "requestClass": "Code",
691: "agentReview": {
692:   "status": "Pass", "otherNotes": null,
693:   "correctness": 0.9875, "completeness": 1,
